# A Strassen-like algorithm already
# written in an alternative basis, so its entries are ninths rather than 0 and
# +/-1. It equals the product of the 7x4 and 4x4 matrices commented out beside
# it.
#
# This is the case where counting nonzeros in floating point goes wrong: the
# entries are exact ninths, and a double never holds one.
shape 7 4
 4/9  -8/9  -8/9  -4/9
   0   5/9     0  10/9
 8/9  -2/3     0     0
 4/9   2/9   8/9   4/9
   0 -10/9     0     0
 4/9  -1/3  -8/9   2/3
-4/9  -2/9   8/9   4/9
